                                       1 Introduction
                                       Vegetables are a major source of vitamins, minerals, dietary fiber, and phytochemicals
                                       such as bioactive peptides, flavonoids, and phenolic compounds, which constitute an
                                       important portion of the diet in various cultures [1, 2]. Therefore, vegetables play an
                                       important role in nutrition all over the world, and their consumption has received more
                                       attention in recent decades due to the trend towards healthy lifestyle [3, 4]. In addition,
                                       the properties of vegetables and their health benefits is considered and international


