38:The Paleo Foundation operates from Cyprus. EU database-rights law provides stronger protection for curated databases than US equivalents. This is a structural advantage to design around, not incidental. Terms of service, access controls, and commercial licensing will leverage this. Claude sessions should preserve per-claim provenance (which source page supports which wiki claim) so that if any source is later withdrawn or contested, the wiki can be re-derived from its source pages without silent data contamination.
90:This build is a compiled wiki, not a query-time RAG surface. Queries may read raw files when needed, but the default goal of ingest is to compile durable knowledge once into source pages, evidence registers, routed wiki pages, and generated public outputs so the same work does not need to be rediscovered from scratch on every question.
124:1. File watcher: a `chokidar` watcher on `wiki/sources/` triggers a rebuild within seconds of any source page being created or modified. Runs as part of `npm run serve`.
130:The model writes the source page. It fills in frontmatter accurately, especially the `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, and `jurisdictions` arrays, because those arrays are the routing layer's input. If a source touches infant formula generally without specifying soy vs non-soy, the frontmatter should say `matrices: [infant-formula]`, not `matrices: [infant-formula-powder-non-soy]`. The routing layer fans broad scopes out to sibling pages; the model does not pre-decide that fan-out by overspecifying frontmatter.
136:The routing layer's output feeds the synthesis workflow in Part 9. When the audit reports that an (ingredient, metal) cell has accumulated a new contributing source, the synthesis pass reads the contributing sources together and updates the ingredient page's `contamination_profile`. The model writes source pages during ingest and runs synthesis as a separate workflow; the routing audit is what connects the two.
176:- **Initial population** (first two sources): read both source pages in full; compute `typical_ppb`, `p95_ppb`, `n_studies: 2`, `confidence: low`; update the cell to `status: populated`; log the event to `data/evidence/review_events.jsonl`.
225:Published third-party testing (Consumer Reports, HBBF, etc.) can be cited as sources, and their methodology can be discussed, but do not reproduce their brand-level tables into the wiki. Link to the source page instead.
269:**Provenance gaps:** wiki claims that do not trace to a specific source page. Every numerical claim in the wiki must link to a source; claims without provenance are a lint failure.

